Puzzles: the Lichess puzzle database (https://database.lichess.org/#puzzles), by lichess.org,
released under CC0 1.0. The Pack in tool/src/main/assets/pack/ is built from the dump of
2026-09-09 (docs/pack.md).

Opening book: games from the Lichess standard rated games database
(https://database.lichess.org/#standard_games), by lichess.org, released under CC0 1.0. The Book in
tool/src/main/assets/book/ is built from the January 2018 dump (docs/book.md).

Pieces: original drawings made for Chess (two sets), released under CC0 1.0 (no rights reserved).
The waiver is CC0 1.0 Universal, in art/pieces/LICENSE.txt.

The APK is built on Light's SDK (https://github.com/lightphone/light-sdk), MIT licence,
Copyright (c) 2026 The Light Phone. The SDK and the Tool bring these libraries into the APK (its
release runtime classpath):

- Apache License 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0): the Kotlin standard library,
  kotlinx.coroutines, kotlinx.serialization, kotlinx-io, Jetpack Compose and AndroidX (including
  Room, DataStore, WorkManager and Media3), Material Components for Android, Ktor, OkHttp, Okio,
  Gson, Guava, Tink, the UnifiedPush Android connector, JSpecify, and the JetBrains and Error Prone
  annotations.
- BSD 3-Clause: Protocol Buffers, JSR 305 annotations.
- MIT: SLF4J API.

The APK leaves out what Light's SDK brings only for its QR code scanner, which Chess never shows:
ML Kit barcode scanning, CameraX, Google Play services, Firebase components and Google's Data
Transport. None of them ships (decision log T1).

